    <string name="paywall_evidence_body">In a controlled weight-loss trial, people who kept a daily food record lost about twice as much weight as those on the same programme who did not (Hollis et al., Am J Prev Med, 2008). Reviews of self-monitoring find the same pattern: the people who write it down get further.</string>
